        <div class="instructions-section">
            <h6><b>INSTRUCTIONS TO INVIGILATORS</b></h6>
            <table style="width: 100%; border:none;">

                <tr>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;"><b>I CIA</b></td>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;">Session I</td>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;">Session II</td>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;">Session III</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;"><b>Examination Timings:</b></td>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;">Forenoon: 9:00 AM</td>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;">Afternoon: 11:30 AM</td>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;">Afternoon: 2:00 PM</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;"><b>Reporting Time:</b></td>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;">Forenoon: 8:30 AM</td>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;">Afternoon: 11:00 AM</td>
                    <td style="border:none; padding: 2px;">Afternoon: 1:30 PM</td>
                </tr>
            </table>

            <h6><b>Invigilator Duties and Responsibilities</b></h6>
            <p>You are kindly requested to adhere to the following guidelines to ensure the smooth and fair conduct of the examinations:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Invigilators are expected to enter the examination hall at least 15 minutes prior to the commencement of the session.</li>
                <li>Candidates must be instructed to leave manuals, notebooks, guides, programmable calculators, and all electronic devices outside the examination hall.</li>
                <li>Please stand at the entrance of the examination hall to verify and allow entry only to candidates possessing valid ID Card.</li>
                <li>Lead the prayer before the commencement of the examination</li>
                <li>Ensure that absolute silence is maintained inside the examination hall at all times.</li>
                <li>After the candidates are seated, distribute the answer booklets and instruct them to carefully write their roll number and subject code.</li>
                <li>No candidate should be permitted to enter the examination hall 15 minutes after the examination has started.</li>
                <li>
                    Take attendance 15 minutes after the commencement of the examination.

                </li>
                <li>Verify that the Roll number on the candidate's ID card matches the number written on their answer sheet.</li>
                <li>Any instance of malpractice should be reported immediately to the Chief Superintendent.</li>
                <li>The use of mobile phones by invigilators during examination duty is strictly prohibited.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>Your cooperation and support in ensuring a smooth and disciplined examination process are highly appreciated.</p>
            <p class="text-center">Thanking you,</p>
